WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.512 --> 00:00:20.714
couldn't bear the thought of upsetting Ray with Alpha's constant squawking.

2
00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:27.017
He had given her so much—a job, delicious meals, a place to live.

3
00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:32.220
"I have to move," she told herself.

4
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:35.009
"I can't stay here much longer."

5
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.671
She spent the whole week looking for a place that she could afford.

6
00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:50.133
She finally found a room to rent in a boardinghouse.

7
00:00:50.153 --> 00:00:53.834
"I'll take it," Ally said to the landlord.

8
00:00:53.854 --> 00:00:55.314
"When can I move in?"

9
00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:59.895
"Now, as long as you pay the first month's rent and—" Ram-bam-bop-boop!

10
00:01:00.615 --> 00:01:02.336
Loud music interrupted the landlord.

11
00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:04.606
She cupped her hands over her ears.

12
00:01:04.626 --> 00:01:06.347
"What's that awful noise?"

13
00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.389
"I'm sorry.

14
00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:09.890
It's just my device."

15
00:01:10.451 --> 00:01:12.993
Ally fumbled, trying to turn the volume down on the device.

16
00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:16.156
"It's not working very well, and it does this sometimes."

17
00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:20.340
"Well, then you can forget about renting this room!"

18
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.781
the landlord fumed.

19
00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.883
"This is a quiet house.

20
00:01:24.224 --> 00:01:26.025
We don't allow loud music."

21
00:01:26.045 --> 00:01:28.788
"It's not what you think," Ally said.

22
00:01:30.284 --> 00:01:33.646
But the landlord led her to the front door and slammed it behind her.

23
00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:39.511
Out on the street, Ally pulled Alpha out of her pocket.

24
00:01:39.531 --> 00:01:45.215
"This is the third time you've blurted out noise and ruined our chances of renting a room!"

25
00:01:45.235 --> 00:01:48.317
"Apologies," Alpha said.

26
00:01:48.337 --> 00:01:50.759
"The device is scrambling Alpha's interface."

27
00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:52.500
Ally sighed.

28
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.182
"It's all my fault.

29
00:01:55.822 --> 00:02:01.358
If I were a responsible Astralian, I would have cloaked the pod, and none of this would ever

30
00:02:01.418 --> 00:02:02.198
have happened."

31
00:02:02.218 --> 00:02:08.342
"Astralian wisdom says that mistakes are necessary to learning," Alpha said.

32
00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:11.844
"Thanks for saying that," Ally said.

33
00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:15.046
"But I'm not sure my parents would see it the same way.

34
00:02:15.687 --> 00:02:21.010
Anyway, just to be safe, I'd better power you down anytime we're around humans.

35
00:02:21.531 --> 00:02:23.672
Especially tonight—at the gala."

36
00:02:26.976 --> 00:02:30.919
When Ally arrived at the diner for the gala, Flo and Randy were busy setting up.

37
00:02:34.662 --> 00:02:39.946
They'd placed little vases shaped like rocket ships on the tables and hung up a giant sign: Welcome,

38
00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:41.887
League of Rocket Scientists!

39
00:02:44.249 --> 00:02:46.230
"It looks awesome in here!"

40
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.411
Ally exclaimed.

41
00:02:48.091 --> 00:02:49.973
"You haven't seen the best part."

42
00:02:51.014 --> 00:02:52.094
Flo nudged Randy.

43
00:02:52.695 --> 00:02:54.036
"Show her what you made."

44
00:02:57.192 --> 00:02:58.893
Randy retrieved a tray from the kitchen.

45
00:02:58.913 --> 00:03:02.856
"It's nothing really.

46
00:03:02.876 --> 00:03:05.018
I was just having some fun."

47
00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.861
Ally looked at Randy's creations.

48
00:03:08.881 --> 00:03:10.482
"Wow, Randy!

49
00:03:10.942 --> 00:03:15.926
You've made meatballs look like planets and pastries look like telescopes and computers!"

50
00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:20.049
"Wait until you see the cake he made!"

51
00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:21.010
Flo said.

52
00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.072
"Not yet though," Randy said.

53
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.502
"Let me put the finishing touches on it first."

54
00:03:27.522 --> 00:03:30.463
"I can't wait," Ally said.

55
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:32.664
"I'll go wash my hands in the restroom.

56
00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:36.507
Then I'll help you finish preparing the food and decorations, Flo."

57
00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:43.590
By the time Ally returned to the dining room, Mateo had arrived.

58
00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.453
"I left gifts all over town for Bethany," he was explaining to Randy and Flo.

59
00:03:48.473 --> 00:03:53.396
"So far she's found an action figure and a pack of Cosmic Quest trading cards.

60
00:03:54.208 --> 00:03:57.990
Hopefully she's on her way to the comics bookstore for her next present and clue."

61
00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.731
"Where will the final clue lead her?"

62
00:04:01.231 --> 00:04:01.951
Flo asked.

63
00:04:01.971 --> 00:04:05.913
"To the red heart sculpture," Mateo replied.

64
00:04:05.933 --> 00:04:07.974
"That's where I'll give her the T-shirt.

65
00:04:08.374 --> 00:04:11.975
But after she figures out the clue at the bookshop, she'll come here to find the clue in

66
00:04:11.995 --> 00:04:12.676
the bathroom.

67
00:04:13.636 --> 00:04:14.736
I'd better get out of here!

68
00:04:15.597 --> 00:04:17.438
I don't want her to find me until the end."

69
00:04:17.458 --> 00:04:22.059
"Will you be back in time for the gala?"

70
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:23.120
Ally asked.

71
00:04:23.884 --> 00:04:24.684
"I hope so!"

72
00:04:26.005 --> 00:04:28.986
Mateo hurried out the back door just as Bethany came in the front.

73
00:04:29.006 --> 00:04:33.907
"Oh, hi, Bethany!"

74
00:04:34.527 --> 00:04:36.568
Ally tried to act surprised to see Bethany.

75
00:04:36.588 --> 00:04:38.248
"What are you doing here?"

76
00:04:38.268 --> 00:04:44.150
"I'm on a scavenger hunt," Bethany replied in a flat voice.

77
00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.110
"A clue led me here."

78
00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.511
"What is it?"

79
00:04:48.911 --> 00:04:49.491
Ally asked.

80
00:04:50.632 --> 00:04:55.294
Bethany recited Mateo's riddle: "'Give me a tap and I'll give you some suds.

81
00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.336
I come in handy when you're covered in mud.'"

82
00:04:58.956 --> 00:05:02.459
Then she added sadly, "The answer is soap."

83
00:05:03.539 --> 00:05:04.320
Ally peered at her.

84
00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.601
"Are you okay?"

85
00:05:09.123 --> 00:05:10.964
Bethany shrugged and headed for the restroom.

86
00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.486
"Huh," Ally thought.

87
00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:15.367
"She seems upset."

88
00:05:16.468 --> 00:05:18.389
Ally did a quick scan of Bethany's mind.

89
00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:21.451
"Oh no!"

90
00:05:21.991 --> 00:05:22.472
Ally thought.

91
00:05:23.884 --> 00:05:28.286
"Bethany is upset about something—she thinks Mateo likes me!

92
00:05:29.707 --> 00:05:30.988
This is terrible!"

93
00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:32.868
Ally paced around.

94
00:05:33.309 --> 00:05:37.931
When Bethany came out, Ally had to find a way to reassure her that Mateo and Ally were

95
00:05:38.011 --> 00:05:38.871
just good friends.

96
00:05:39.532 --> 00:05:42.793
But before Bethany was back, Ray called Ally into the kitchen.

97
00:05:43.474 --> 00:05:47.996
And by the time Ally was finished helping him stack water glasses, Bethany was gone.
